// trap: two `@null` columns that both hold null are not equal, so `!=` holds and `==` fails (#355).
// The model of #355, without its labels. Nothing writes qty or lim, so the Item that Make
// creates holds null in both. The language reference (§ Null) says a null column satisfies
// no comparison with a column and satisfies every `!=`, as the SQL CHECKs read it: qty !=
// lim holds and qty == lim fails on the new row, so Make breaks both rules in its first
// step. An engine that read null == null as true would answer ok for both and z3 would
// prove them. BFS refutes both, so the proof does not try them; proof_equivalence checks
// that z3 would not prove them.
// expect Forbidden_Item_0: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample z3=refuted
// expect Required_Item_0: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample z3=refuted
entity Item "品目" {
  id: Int @pk
  qty: Int @null
  lim: Int @null
}
usecase Make "作成"
creates(Make, Item)
forbidden(Item, qty != lim)
required(Item, qty == lim)
